#!/usr/bin/env bash
# Refuses an AI-attribution trailer in a commit message.
#
# The rule is the owner's, from 2026-09-24: no `Co-Authored-By: Claude …`, nor
# any other AI attribution trailer, in a commit message or a PR description. The
# work is the person's who directed it.
#
# It needs a gate because the rule alone did not hold. Measured 2026-11-22 over
# the whole history: **810** such trailers, and they were still arriving —
# 126 in August, 83 in September, 443 in October, 136 in November, the most
# recent five days before this hook was written. A rule that every session is
# free to forget is a rule that the contributors page quietly contradicts.
#
# Install: `make bootstrap`, or `git config core.hooksPath .githooks`.
# Bypass:  `git commit --no-verify` (git's own, deliberately left alone).
set -euo pipefail

msg_file=${1:?commit-msg hook: no message file}

# Vendor domains, never NAMES. `Claude` is a common first name, and refusing a
# human co-author called Claude would be a false positive in the one place a
# false positive costs the most — someone's credit. Every one of the 810 found
# in this history carries `<noreply@anthropic.com>`, so the domain is enough.
AI_DOMAINS='anthropic\.com|openai\.com|users\.noreply\.github\.com/copilot'

# Ask GIT what a trailer is, instead of grepping the body. A message may NAME
# the trailer while explaining the rule — the commit that introduced the
# `.mailmap` does exactly that — and a grep would refuse it. `interpret-trailers
# --parse` returns only what a parser (git's, GitHub's) would act on.
trailers=$(git interpret-trailers --parse <"$msg_file" 2>/dev/null || true)
[ -n "$trailers" ] || exit 0

offenders=$(printf '%s\n' "$trailers" | grep -Ei "$AI_DOMAINS" || true)
[ -n "$offenders" ] || exit 0

cat >&2 <<EOF
commit-msg: refused — AI attribution trailer

$(printf '%s\n' "$offenders" | sed 's/^/    /')

The rule (CLAUDE.md, 2026-09-24): a commit message carries no
\`Co-Authored-By: Claude …\`, nor any other AI attribution trailer. The work
belongs to whoever directed it, and the contributors page counts a co-author
trailer as a person.

Remove the line(s) and commit again. If you are sure, \`git commit --no-verify\`.
EOF
exit 1
